            <fr:title text="Equivalences">Equivalences</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Type Theory</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
    This note follows Chapter 9 of <fr:link href="/hott-2022/" title="Introduction to Homotopy Type Theory" uri="https://caimeo.space/hott-2022/" display-uri="hott-2022" type="local">Introduction to Homotopy Type Theory</fr:link>.
    Equivalence is the correct notion of sameness between types; its definition must eventually be
    shown to be a property of a map rather than extra, non-unique structure.
</html:p>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors />
                <fr:date>
